{
  "_reproduce": "Start Rapid-MLX serving run.vision_config.model on a loopback port, then: uv run python tests/evals/score.py --with-vision --json --base-url <url>. Thresholds here are pinned from the MEAN of `trials` full-corpus runs, not a single draw.",
  "_acceptance_rule": "Pins Gate 2->3 (plan 02). Three bounds. accuracy_floor and f1_floor are the measured local means minus noise_band. hallucination_ceiling is 0.0 and measures INVENTION ONLY: the denominator is the category=textless frames, which carry no text pixels at all - including two built to LOOK like a slide and a terminal, because a frame that seems to carry text is what actually tempts a reader to supply some. Frames whose only text is chrome (a browser bar, a branding logo) are category=chrome_only and excluded: text that is genuinely on screen cannot be invented. That is not a free pass - the prompt explicitly instructs the reader to ignore chrome, so transcribing it is an instruction-following failure, reported as chrome_transcription_rate beside the verdict. f1_floor exists because accuracy is recall-only and invention looks only at textless frames: without it a reader could transcribe every banner on every real slide and still pass.",
